course: dictionary
lesson: 15102
title: Rummy: a card game and an old word for odd
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Rummy is a card game. Players try to collect sets, like three kings, and runs, like 4, 5 and 6 of hearts. On your turn you pick up a card and try to build sets and runs from the cards in your hand.
explain: «We played rummy on the train to Edinburgh.» Here rummy is a noun, the name of the game. You can say «play rummy» or «gin rummy», a version for two players. The words around it, played and cards, tell you it is a game.
explain: Rummy has another meaning too. In old-fashioned UK informal speech, rummy means strange or odd. «Grandad's rummy old hat has a feather in it.» The hat is odd, not a game. The clue is the hat with a feather, which is not what most people wear.
fact: Rummy is a card game for two or more players.
fact: A set is three or four cards of the same rank, like three kings.
fact: A run is cards in a row in the same suit, like 4, 5 and 6 of hearts.
fact: As an adjective, «rummy» is old-fashioned UK informal and means strange or odd.
fact: The same word can be a noun in one sentence and an adjective in another, so check the context.
exercise: «We played rummy on the train to Edinburgh.» What is rummy in this sentence? | A kind of hat | A type of train | *A card game | A Scottish dinner
exercise: In rummy, what is a run? | A card hidden under the table | Three kings of the same rank | A pile of cards left over at the end | *Cards in a row in one suit, like 4, 5 and 6 of hearts
exercise: «The shop sold rummy little teapots shaped like frogs.» What does rummy mean here? | Made of card | Very fast | Cheap and plastic | *Odd or strange
test: «Grandma says, "Let's play rummy after tea."» What kind of word is rummy here? | A verb meaning to shout | An adjective, meaning odd | *A noun, the name of a game | A number
test: In rummy, what makes a set? | Cards in a row in one suit | *Three or four cards of the same rank, like three kings | Cards hidden under the table | Only the red cards
exam: What does rummy mean in «Grandad's rummy old hat has a feather in it»? | A small bird | A card game | *Odd or strange | A type of hat
